Project: Predicting Student Performance Using Data Science
Step-by-Step Process
1. Data Loading & Cleaning
Loaded data from CSV
Checked for missing/null values (none found )
2. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Plotted distribution of grades
Heatmap of correlations to see which features affect G3
Example Insight: studytime and G3 are positively correlated
3.Statistical Analysis
T-test to compare grades of students who go out a lot vs. less
Found that high social activity may reduce academic performance (p-value < 0.05)
4.Feature Engineering
Converted final grade G3 into binary
Encoded categorical (text) data using LabelEncoder
Scaled features using StandardScaler
5.Model Building
Split data into train and test (80-20)
Applied two ML models:Logistic Regression, Random Forest Classifier
6.Model Evaluation
Measured accuracy, precision, recall, and confusion matrix
Random Forest gave higher accuracy than Logistic Regression
7.Final Results
Important factors for passing: studytime, absences, failures, goout
Random Forest was the best-performing model
The project shows how statistics + ML can work together for insights and predictions
Why is this Important?
Helps schools and educators identify at-risk students early.
Supports data-driven decisions for improving education strategies.
Good example of applying real-world data science techniques like EDA, statistics, and ML.
